@normanmaurer I agree, that's why I remove the second one in destroy. 
The first one, in offer, is necessary according to the previous code (the if that preceeds says refCnt > 1, so needing more than one release).
However, note that according to my test (and using no more retained for the first Chunk), even the first one (in offer) could be of no use (never goes within the else part).

